    and those were the only support tickets so far.

  First question: [1mwhat should people be able to narrow by?[0m

  - [1mEvent type[0m: a checkbox list or select of the nine types. It covers the failed sign-in case and most "where's the X
    event" searches. It's cheap, and the list is fixed and safe to hard-code.
  - [1mDate range[0m: two date pickers. Useful, but it brings in time zone handling (a day boundary is in the viewer's zone,
    while the data is in UTC) and validation messages. That's noticeably more code and more guideline surface.
  - [1mText search[0m: one search box matched against device, location, and details. Flexible, but fuzzy, and it doesn't make
    failed sign-ins any easier to spot than a type filter does.

  I'd start with [1mevent type only[0m. It directly solves the documented support problem, keeps the diff small (the notes cap
  it at about 300 lines), and adding date or text filters later doesn't undo any of it. Date range is what I'd add
  second.

